    "summary": "Model complete and passing all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nBridge: single simply-supported span, 30 m bearing-centre-to-centre, 10 m deck (9 m carriageway), two-way, Highway Class II, 2 design lanes. Superstructure: 3 precast prestressed small-box girders (C40), modelled as a 2D spine beam with combined section properties from the middle-girder geometry (single A = 1.139 m², I = 0.3549 m⁴; combined A = 3.417 m², I = 1.065 m⁴; Ec = 32500 MPa; γ = 26 kN/m³; w = 88.84 kN/m; m = 9.056 t/m). Supports: abutments at both ends on plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×400 mm, 5×8 mm layers), 2 per girder end = 6 per line, modelled as zero-length springs (S = 10.71, Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m, rotation free). Live load: qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN, transverse factor ξ = 1.0, impact μ = 0.2006 from f1 = 3.402 Hz.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure: the transverse lane-load factor lane.xi was set to 0.78 (the value for 3 loaded lanes) whereas JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 gives ξ = 1.0 for 2 design lanes. The incorrect factor made the L2 code check on lane-load effects fail; the model-checks wrapper reported it without naming a suspect. Repairing lane.xi to 1.0 (and re-running the modal analysis / re-deciding lane.mu after the instance rewrite cleared f1) made generate_model succeed.\n\nKey results: f1 = 3.402 Hz (1st vertical bending), self-weight reactions 1332.5 kN per support (sum = 2665.1 kN = full self-weight), self-weight mid-span moment 9994 kN·m, maximum lane-load positive moment 6449.6 kN·m."
